  "title": "RBL Bank Q2 FY27 profit nearly triples to Rs 482 crore on loan growth, FCNR(B) gains",
  "summary": "RBL Bank’s advances rose 42 per cent year on year to Rs 1.42 lakh crore and deposits growing 34 per cent to Rs 1.56 lakh crore, while net profit nearly tripled to Rs 482 crore. The headline balance-sheet growth was partly supported by the bank’s mobilisation of Rs 32,472 crore through the RBI’s FCNR(B) swap facility, against which its international banking unit extended Rs 10,309 crore in loans. Excluding loans extended against FCNR(B) deposits, management said underlying loan growth was around 30 per cent, while deposit growth excluding FCNR(B) stood at 6 per cent.",
